## Session-9 standing context

The following findings from the Hu9 analysis session (o46max-8
advisor) are binding context for this session. Ground all
dispatch and triage decisions in them.

### Barrier landscape

Five barrier results constrain the group-theoretic approach:

| Family | Status | Reference |
|--------|--------|-----------|
| Bounded-exponent abelian (STPP) | DEAD | BCCGNS+U 2017, arXiv:1605.06702 |
| Bounded-exponent nilpotent (STPP) | DEAD | BCCGU 2018, arXiv:1712.02302 |
| Groups of Lie type (TPP) | DEAD (can't reach omega < 2+ε) | BCGPU 2022, arXiv:2204.03826 |
| Young subgroups of S_n | DEAD | BCCGU 2018, arXiv:1712.02302 |
| CW_q tensors (universal method) | omega >= 2.168 | Alman 2019, arXiv:1812.08731 |

The Lie type barrier identifies the **second-smallest irrep
dimension** as the key obstruction — directly the alpha < gamma
question. PSL(2,q) are groups of Lie type and are therefore
killed for omega; the Im15/Im16/Im17 sweeps of PSL(2,q) are
structural data only.

The SDPP conjecture (CKSU Conjecture 4.1/4.7, "two-families")
is the **last surviving CKSU conjecture** that would imply
omega = 2. It lives in abelian groups of possibly unbounded
exponent. Pratt 2023 [arXiv:2309.03878] showed its truth would
require large skew corner-free sets, suggesting it may be
false, but the conjecture remains open. An SDPP machinery audit
is in `.tasks/f5exp/docs/Hu9-sdpp-audit.md`.

### The alpha = gamma wall

CU03 proved alpha(C_{2n} wr S_n) -> 2, but this gives **no
omega bound**: the character-degree parameter gamma converges
at the same rate (alpha = gamma), making the capacity
inequality (CKSU Theorem 5.1) trivial. The C_{2n} route was
fully analyzed in CU03 and has not advanced since. Aw1
formalizes a generalization of this known-to-be-insufficient
result.

**The non-abelian case (Pl21) matters because non-abelian
groups can have alpha < gamma** — the character degrees might
grow slowly enough to give a nontrivial omega bound. That is
the open frontier. Prioritize Pl21 and its dependencies
(Ca1, Df1) accordingly.

### Manuscript framing

`Manuscripts/Drafts/abelian-factor-refutation.md` has been
reframed as a contribution to the structural theory of TPP
capacity (the Hedtke-Murthy / Murthy line), not to the
omega = 2 program. The lift law at p = 2 is machine-checked
(`Proofs/Xlib/TPPLift.lean`, sorry-free). The general-p
lift law is not formalized. Hu9 (manuscript sign-off) is
active and awaiting the USER's verdict.

### DAG priority ordering

1. **Pl21** (Clifford, general-H wreath) — highest value;
   the alpha < gamma frontier.
2. **Ca1 / Df1** — prerequisites to Pl21; keep unblocked.
3. **Sq1** — general pseudoExponent convergence; feeds Ca1.
4. **Aw1** — growing abelian base; true but known-insufficient
   for omega. Do not block the critical path on it.
5. **Pl18 downstreams** (Im14-Im17, Pd1, Hu11-12, Pl23) —
   structural data collection; lower priority than the
   formal proof chain.
6. **Pl22 track (S)** — formalizing BCCGNS+U Theorem B;
   strategically interesting, not urgent.

